# Build output
node_modules/
dist/
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/

# Kit archives and the scenes extracted from them. `maps/work/` is 807 MB of
# intermediate `scene.glb` files that `tools/prepare-maps.mjs` writes and reads
# back; the playable maps it produces live in `public/assets/maps/`. The
# archives are re-downloadable from polyfork, the built maps are not.
maps/work/
*.zip

# The extracted Polyfork kit itself — never in the repo.
#
# These trees hold the kit's own source modules (`.mjs`), its authoring
# manifests (`LAYOUT.json`, `PARTS.json`, `KIT.md`) and the raw part meshes.
# Only the `.glb` files are CC BY 4.0; the `.mjs` and the manifests are under
# the Polyfork License, which forbids redistributing them as standalone asset
# files — and a public GitHub repo is exactly that, down to the last commit.
# The game does not need them: it serves the maps `tools/prepare-maps.mjs`
# builds into `public/assets/maps/`, which are CC BY 4.0 and credited in
# `docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`. Re-extract a kit locally when rebuilding one.
assets-source/
extracted_kit/

# Scratch stays out of the repo. One-off harnesses, their logs, their screenshots
# and the Chrome profile the CDP driver opens all start with `tmp-`, so the prefix
# is the rule. A harness worth keeping graduates to `tools/` — `pickable.mjs` and
# `spots.mjs` did.
tmp-*

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
